settings.liquid:
{%- comment -%}
  Claude Code, 2026-08-31 - hero banner CSS for /pages/shipping-returns. Same two
  fixes the contact banner needed, and needed for the same measured reasons.

  1. DESKTOP RIGHT-PIN. The master is 3000x678 (4.425:1) against a box that is a
     fixed 440px height across a full-bleed width, so at 1440 the box is 3.27:1 and
     `cover` drops ~508px of width. Centred, half comes off the RIGHT - the side
     carrying the carton, her hands and the driver. Pinned right, the crop only
     ever removes extended hallway.

  2. MOBILE TOP SCRIM. The mobile master is a face-and-parcel crop with no dark
     band for the heading, and this page's heading is followed by a subheading
     ("Free shipping within Europe..."), so it needs MORE clear space than contact
     did, not less. Contrast is bought with a local scrim behind the type, never by
     raising the section overlay - a flatter overlay dims the photograph to fix the
     heading, which is the trade this project has already rejected once. The ramp
     runs slightly deeper than contact's for the second line.

  Scoped with {{ section.id }} rather than the section class, so it cannot land on
  another image-with-text-overlay if one is ever added to this template.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
@media screen and (min-width: 700px) {
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .content-over-media > picture > img,
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .content-over-media > img { object-position: right center; }
}

@media screen and (max-width: 699px) {
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .content-over-media::before {
    background-image: linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(26, 26, 26, 0.90) 0%, rgba(26, 26, 26, 0.72) 34%, rgba(26, 26, 26, 0.00) 70%);
  }
}

/* The theme wraps a liquid block in a plain <div>, which takes a gap in the text
   stack and pushes the heading off centre. The style inside still applies while
   its wrapper is display:none. */
#shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .prose > div:has(> style) { display: none; }
</style>
<style>
/* Claude Code, 2026-08-31 - reduce the /pages/shipping-returns banner height.

   RE-APPLIED. This rule was published earlier today against a hero that had NO
   image, as a flat 280/300/340 ladder. A concurrent session then published the
   parcel photograph and rewrote this whole hero_css block with its right-pin and
   mobile scrim, which silently dropped the height rules - the banner went back to
   440px. Appended here rather than replacing, so that session's two fixes survive
   this one the way this one did not survive theirs.

   And the number had to change, because the hero is no longer empty. A fixed
   340px against the new 4.42:1 master is fine at 1512 but crops vertically as the
   viewport widens, which is how the contact banner lost the top of a head. So the
   height follows the master's ratio instead: the box matches the picture at every
   desktop width, crop stays near zero, and it is still much shorter - 342px at
   1512 against the 440px it is on now. At 440 the box is 3.44:1 against a 4.42:1
   master, so cover was throwing away 22% of the image WIDTH - the side carrying
   the carton, her hands and the driver. Shortening the box is what puts them back
   in frame.

   Mobile is deliberately NOT reduced, for the same reason as contact: below 700px
   a 0.944:1 face-and-parcel crop sits in a 1.040:1 box and is already cropped 9%
   vertically, which is what the scrim above exists for. Shortening it crops her
   further. */
@media screen and (min-width: 700px) {
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .content-over-media {
    --content-over-media-height: max(280px, calc(100vw / 4.42));
  }
}
</style>
